language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ clock_triplets: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Rearrange the numbers 1 to 12 on the face of a clock so that no triplet of adjacent numbers has a sum higher than 21. The positions go round the clock, so position 12 is adjacent to positions 11 and 1.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/clock_triplets.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ x[p]: the number at clock position p, p = 1 to 12 going round the clock (position 1 is the first, as the data is 1-based)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..12)] of int(1..12)

such that
$ every number from 1 to 12 appears exactly once on the clock
allDiff(x),
$ no triplet of adjacent positions has a sum higher than 21, for every position p with the two positions after it going round the clock
forAll p : int(1..12) . x[p] + x[(p % 12) + 1] + x[((p + 1) % 12) + 1] <= 21
